# An exception handler `(e) -> { unwind(v) }` is a closure whose body is
# trial-evaluated at definition time, and the trial SWALLOWS what it throws.
# An `unwind` value whose type is not the enclosing fn's return type was
# swallowed with it: `yo check` passed, `yo compile` exited 0, and the handler
# became an abort() stub that fired the first time the handler ran
# (issues/fixed/unwind-type-mismatch-in-a-handler-is-swallowed.md). Both
# types are concrete, so the mismatch is now re-raised: rc=1 and the E0604.
# `comptime_expect_error` cannot pin a swallow, so the gate is `yo check`.
stdout_keep_match=(error\[E0604\]: Incompatible type for .unwind. argument|Expected \(enclosing function return type\): i32|Got: unit)
